1. Why are the rounded and explicitly cast integer results sometimes different?
Because rounded integers round to the nearest ten, while explicitly cast integers do not round the decimal.
2. Which result would be more appropriate for an official grade report, and why?
Rounded grades are more appropriate because truncated grades lower the value, and it is important to acknowledge the decimal value of a student's grade. 
3. What role does implicit type conversion play when multiplying scores by decimal weights?
It avoids problems when multiplying a whole number without a decimal point, which could otherwise produce incorrect answers. 
